/*!
\page page_stkinkvertex StKinkVertex

\brief Vertex representing a kink decay: one charged parent decaying to one charged daughter.

\section stkinkvertex_overview Overview
StKinkVertex reconstructs the decay vertex of K± → μ±ν and π± → μ±ν (and similar)
topologies.  The parent track (accessed via StVertex::parent()) ends at the kink
vertex; the daughter track (daughter()) starts there.  Decay angles and DCA
quantities for topology selection are stored directly.

Kink vertices are stored in StEvent::kinkVertices().

\section stkinkvertex_hierarchy Class Hierarchy
\code{.cpp}
TObject → StObject → StMeasuredPoint → StVertex → StKinkVertex
\endcode

\section stkinkvertex_datamembers Data Members

| Member | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| mDaughter | StLink<StTrack> | Non-owning link to daughter track. |
| mParentGeantId | UShort_t | GEANT ID of the parent. |
| mDaughterGeantId | UShort_t | GEANT ID of the daughter. |
| mDcaParentDaughter | Float_t | Parent–daughter DCA at kink (cm). |
| mDecayAngleCM | Float_t | Decay angle in parent rest frame (rad). |
| mDecayAngle | Float_t | Decay angle in lab frame (rad). |
| mParentMomentum | StThreeVectorF | Parent momentum at kink vertex (GeV/c). |
| mDaughterMomentum | StThreeVectorF | Daughter momentum at kink vertex (GeV/c). |
| mDeltaEnergy[3] | Float_t | dE for three decay hypotheses. |

\section stkinkvertex_methods Key Methods

\code{.cpp}
const StSPtrVecKinkVertex& kinks = event->kinkVertices();
for (size_t i = 0; i < kinks.size(); ++i) {
    const StKinkVertex* kink = kinks[i];
    float angleCM = kink->decayAngleCM();  // rad - use for K/pi ID
    const StThreeVectorF& pP = kink->parentMomentum();
    const StThreeVectorF& pD = kink->daughterMomentum();
}
\endcode

\sa \ref page_stvertex, \ref page_stv0vertex
*/
